# a constraint whose values the new alternatives may cover together: the
# checker finds no value of the prior constraint that new rejects, and does not
# combine alternatives, so it cannot decide (beside
# disjunction-narrowed-to-values)
-- old.cue --
r!: =~"^(a|b)$"
b!: bool
-- new.cue --
r!: "a" | "b"
b!: true | false
-- out --
unknown
b is now true | false, no single alternative of which covers the prior alternative bool; the checker does not combine alternatives (rule unknown-disjunction) @ new.cue:2:1
r is now "a" | "b", no single alternative of which covers the prior alternative =~"^(a|b)$"; the checker does not combine alternatives (rule unknown-disjunction) @ new.cue:1:1
